{"id":"antiderivatives","title":"Four antiderivatives","difficulty":"core","chapter":"substitution","topics":["integration","substitution"],"scope":"ab","promptHtml":"<p>Give an antiderivative of each. The constant of integration is optional — any\ncorrect antiderivative is accepted, since they all differ by a constant.</p>\n","parts":[{"prompt":"∫ 6x² dx","reference":"2*x**3","mode":"antiderivative","variable":"x","positive":""},{"prompt":"∫ x·e^(x²) dx","reference":"exp(x**2)/2","mode":"antiderivative","variable":"x","positive":""},{"prompt":"∫ 1/(x + 3) dx","reference":"log(x + 3)","mode":"antiderivative","variable":"x","positive":""},{"prompt":"∫ sin(x)·cos(x) dx","reference":"sin(x)**2/2","mode":"antiderivative","variable":"x","positive":""}],"hints":[],"solutionNotesHtml":"<p><strong>Always differentiate your answer.</strong> Every rejection below would have been\ncaught in seconds by doing so, and it is the only check available on an exam.</p>\n<p>The last problem is the interesting one. Three <em>different-looking</em> answers are\nall accepted:</p>\n<p class=\"katex-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"/><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"/><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{\\sin^2 x}{2}, \\qquad -\\frac{\\cos^2 x}{2}, \\qquad -\\frac{\\cos 2x}{4}\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.2349em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></s